winemac.drv: export the macdrv_functions table DXMT's winemetal.so looks up.

Runner B (steamplay-mac), stage B2. DXMT's unix side (src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c,
3Shain/dxmt 7c8dee1 and v0.80) creates its CAMetalLayer with
dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, "macdrv_functions") and falls back to dlsym of get_win_data,
release_win_data, macdrv_view_create_metal_view and macdrv_view_get_metal_layer. Upstream Wine
builds winemac.so with hidden visibility, so neither is found and DXMT gets a device but no
swapchain. CrossOver exports the table; upstream does not.

New file dlls/winemac.drv/dxmt_export.c exports the table with default visibility. It is a port
of leonseemann/NotProton winemac-patch/dxmt_export.c (GPL-3, written for Wine 11.15; commit
d56e28e0, file sha256 66056ac563453a64...) to the wine-11.18 winemac API:
- macdrv_CreateClientSurface() takes (hwnd, pixel_format, raw); called as (hwnd, 0, FALSE),
  the arguments win32u's Vulkan path uses;
- macdrv_window / macdrv_view / macdrv_metal_{device,view,layer} are now WineWindow,
  WineContentView, id_MTLDevice, WineMetalView and CAMetalLayer;
- a NULL 10th slot (on_main_thread) so the table is as large as DXMT's struct; DXMT never
  calls it.
DXMT reads slots 1 (get_win_data), 2 (release_win_data), 6 (view_create_metal_view),
7 (view_get_metal_layer) and 8 (view_release_metal_view), and only client_cocoa_view from the
win data. ntdll dlopens unix libraries with RTLD_NOW, which is RTLD_GLOBAL on macOS, so
dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT) finds the table.

Licence: dxmt_export.c is GPL-3.0 (attribution kept in the file); winemac.so built with it is
distributed under the GPL-3.0 as a whole. The Makefile.in hunk is LGPL-2.1-or-later like the
file it changes.

Known limitation (same as the 11.15 original): the client surface made on demand is not on
win32u's surface lists, so it is not detached or freed before the window is destroyed.

Written against wine-11.18 (tag wine-11.18, commit 7b3fff76f). Upstream status: none; drop if
DXMT or upstream winemac grow another way to reach the client view.

